A||N||6||87MaroonGTKCMO||Considering a Fiero purchase (becoming a repeat buyer/owner)||||5||
Z||000000||87MaroonGTKCMO||01-05-2001||09:04 PM||||Hi,<P>My name is Sean and I used to have a Red 84 SE Fiero that was stolen when I moved from Wichita, KS to Kansas City, MO.  Unfortunately the car was too damaged for me to repair, so I traded it in on a new car. However, I saw a Maroon 87 GT today with over 200K on the clock.  This has gotten me back into the spirit of wanting to purchase a Fiero again. I have never owned a V-6 Fiero or a fastback before.  Let me describe the car to you all.<P>Fastback<BR>New Tires<BR>New Maroon paint (Some overspray in door jam)<BR>Owner painted the shift cover trim and Instrument panel trim in the same exterior paint.<BR>Dark Grey Interior.<BR>5 Spd Getrag.<BR>Wing.<BR>No Defrost.<BR>Subwoofer Performance Sound & Slider.<BR>Power Windows.<BR>Power Locks.<BR>Power Mirrors<BR>No scratches in Door or Fastback glass.<BR>Small crack in Side Marker lite and fender.<BR>Rear taillights have no swirl marks or fade.<BR>Non-functioning headlight motors<BR>Parking brake handle wouldn't pull up<BR>Trunk release (Wouldn't work) possible fuse?<BR>Wierd seat fabric (black, felt like shoe canvas, is this suede? It had the Fiero Logos in the back of seats.)<BR>CD Player. Terrible sound<BR>NO sunroof.<BR>Headliner O.K.<BR>Check Engine never came on.<BR>Diamond Spoke wheels.<BR>Started right up, no Tick or Knock or Smoke.<BR>Idled Down at Warmup.<P>Dealer won't let drive unless I am serious to buy it.<BR>Asking price $1800 US dollars. I about fainted. Never seen one that low before. If it wasn't for Property Taxes this month, I think I would have bought it by now.<P>Any comments or questions that you think I am overlooking here?  Small Loans accepted!<P>||||reg||5
Z||000001||TheFiero64||01-06-2001||09:37 AM||||Welcome to the Forum <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I think you should get it. That is a low price. You better do something and act fast.<BR><P>------------------<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fformula88||01-06-2001||10:54 AM||||It doesn't sound too bad but if you make an offer, go considerably lower than the asking price to start.  No matter what conditiona car is in, 200K is a LOT of miles.  But that doesn't make it a bad buy, just one that should be fairly cheap.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">  <BR>1988 Fiero Formula||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||01-06-2001||12:32 PM||||The fact that he won't let you drive it unless you come up with a down payment is stupid. He can let you drive it! This is just his way of gaining control over the situation and it's another sales tactic scam. He can judge how badly you want this car by your reaction to not being able to drive it unless you give him a deposit. If you told him that you want to drive it before you mad an offer and if not the deal is off he would probably have let you driven the car and thought to himself this guy is not going to be easy. If he didn’t let you drive it than I would have walked off the lot.<P>The GT fiero you described sounds like it is in a little rough shape although that is subject to each persons interpretation of rough shape and there are no pictures. The person that owned this car has obviously taken parts of this car apart and in my opinion a well taken care of virgin car has the most value, not a customized car done to someone else’s taste. People that customize there cars and take them apart could have done anything to it that you won’t find out until you have been driving it for six months.  <P>You should have someone you know like a mechanic go over this car from the engine to the body looking for any more signs of tampering and to see if there are any signs of an accident like paint overspray or different color body parts. You should also run the car’s VIN number on one of those web-sites that tell you the cars registration history. I would definitely offer him a lower price than $1800 based on what you find about the car’s condition. If he won't come down in price, let you test drive the car, or there is something you find wrong like the car was in an accident, than walk away. I think it is better to pay more for a nice car than it is to pay a little for a piece of crap that will only suck your wallet dry in the end and give you a big headache. <P> Have patience and keep looking because this car may not be the one for you.<BR>||||reg||1
